After reading a recent Lycanthrope YAAP, I decided it was time to
renew my Slashem membership card. ;)

So I downloaded Windows SlashEM tty Alpha Version 0.0.7E3, and
started Oz, the lycan undead slayer.

On level 4, I found a ring of polymorph control, which solved
a major problem.  There was also a gauntlets of power and a
cloak of MR (opera) on that level, due to an armor shop, which
regrettably only offered rustproofing.

With the [GoP worn to boost my damage, I was soon in minetown,
which was cross-aligned.  I found a magic lamp there in the
candle shop, which a summoned wolf was happy to liberate for me.
First wish was for +2 SDSM, to replace my mithril.

I continued down (undead level), and picked up a luckstone and
healthstone, then headed back up.  A couple of shop identifies
of valuble gems, a little sale, and 5 points of purchased
protection.

Back on level 3 there was a cross-aligned altar, which I converted.
There was also a weapon shop which offered both enchanting and
poisoning.  A short sacfest netted both the magnificent Bat from Hell,
which became my primary weapon, followed by the Wallet of Perseus.

I had become expert in dagger, and had collected about 16 of them,
so I had them enchanted to +3 and poisoned.  Combined with the [GoP,
they provided a powerful ranged attack.  My starting pistol was
handy for practice.

I skipped most of Sokoban, since I already had holding and reflection.
I only searched the first two levels for rings/wands and ?oEarth.

A bit deeper in the dungeon, I found the Orcish caverns, with a new
map.  I waited a bit to solve that one.

The beholder level was easy with my daggers, and Vecna's level was easy
with a wand of fireball, a lich summoned cockatrice, and the Bat from Hell.
An arch-lich was kind enough to drop the +3 Magicbane, and the Hand of
Vecna effectively doubled my hitpoints.

I went back and did the quest, using the Bat from Hell, which was a little
foolish, since Dracula did some serious damage.  But I managed to survive.

A small group of soldiers I encountered gifted me with a submachine gun
and about 150 bullets.  I rapidly progressed to expert in firearms.

I went back to the black market, where a randomly generated hill giant
tossed a boulder at me.  After killing the giant, I pushed the boulder
to the free space in front of the door, jumped outside the shop, and
gunned down One Eye'd Sam twice in cold blood. I ditched my SDSM and
used Sam's [SoR, then enchanted up my shimmering scales.

A wish from a blessed potion of full healing went for speed boots, which
obviously meant that I would find two pairs just lying on the floor soon
after.

Medusa was petrified by her reflection, and I progressed on to the castle.
I used a cockatrice corpse to eliminate most of the soldiers before they
could use their ammo.  A short smashing/cancelling session and I had 
about 750 bullets, which I poisoned and enchanted to +6. I also switched
my submachine gun with an assault rifle which I enchanted to +6.

I went back and cleared some more levels.  This eventually exposed a
portal to Croesus's castle.  The door was smashed open, so I used a
scroll of earth to hide from the crowd, then I pulled out my assault
rifle and blasted the helpless crowd into oblivion.  After I smashed
the door to the castle with a wand of striking, I used the rifle
again to clean out the insides.

I was getting a little carried away with the rock-and-roll, so I
decided to visit Von Helsing and go postal.  My quest leader and
his minions were wiped away (along with my pious alignment) in a
hail of poisoned lead.  A quick trip to a co-aligned priest
and a 600*XL donation and all was forgiven.

A couple of reverse-geno's of tengus were required to gain teleport
control, and afterwards I decided to free up a ring slot by eating
rings of polycontrol.  I collected three rings, and was willing to
eat two, but the first one gave me the critical intrinsic.

I'd found that silver rings were teleport control, so I decided to
try a new Stupid ascension trick and kill Demogorgon barehanded.
Not much of a challenge for an undead slayer, but good for laughs.

Getting bored with writing this.

After bringing the amulet to DLVL 1, I decided to use up my teleport
scrolls and clear out Frankenstein's level, which I had noted the stairs
for but didn't bother visiting on the way down.  I tamed the monster,
and gunned down the good doctor.  I tried to bring him through the
Planes with me, but he didn't survive.  I should have revived him,
but I didn't think of it until it was too late.

I drained and tamed Famine and Pest on the astral plane, then I
tamed a dragon, wished up a saddle and ascended with 9 pets.

All in all, Slashem is even cooler than it was four years ago when I last
ascended.

